      "caveat": "Every KRAS mutation call in the cohort's samples, one row per call; uncalled mutations are left out, as the portal leaves them out. Structural variants with KRAS as either partner are rows too, as the portal's Mutations tab lists them: type Fusion, the protein change built from their genes, no allele counts or Genome Nexus columns; their annotation is the pair's OncoKB call in the sample's tumour type, their driver status the pair's call with no tumour type (as the portal asks each), or the partners' gene-level Fusion calls where the pair has none stored. Annotation is OncoKB v7.5 (oncogenicity and its highest sensitivity level for the gene). HGVSc, Functional Impact, gnomAD, ClinVar, dbSNP and SIGNAL are Genome Nexus GRCh37 2.2.3-vep116-clinvar20260208+f2, GRCh38 1.4.1-vepNA-clinvar20250106+f2, read from the offline store; HGVSc and SIFT, PolyPhen-2 and AlphaMissense are on the canonical transcript of KRAS (MSKCC overrides). Genome Nexus's GRCh38 service has no SIGNAL, so it is empty for a GRCh38 study; gnomAD and dbSNP are blank for the few variants Genome Nexus cannot serve myvariant.info's record of. Not yet annotated, so blank in those columns: msk_chord_2024. Allele frequency is variant reads over variant + reference reads; # Mut in Sample is the study's own MUTATION_COUNT, blank where it records none. Showing 1,373 of 2,411 mutations: rows Protein Change matches /^G1[23]/; Allele Freq (T) ≥ 0.2. Sorted by Allele Freq (T) (highest first), missing values last, across the cohort; every page is a slice of that one order, and the download holds every row kept, with every column. ",
      "method": {
        "steps": [
          {
